    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Backend.Group">Firewall backend</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Backend.Compatibility">Windows Firewall Compatibility</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Backend.Wfp">GeniaFirewall WFP — standalone inbound/outbound backend</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Backend.Info">The WFP backend applies rules directly through GeniaFirewall.Service at ALE_AUTH_CONNECT and ALE_AUTH_RECV_ACCEPT for IPv4/IPv6 TCP/UDP. In Normal mode unsolicited inbound traffic is blocked by default; EnableAll and IncomingOnly can permit inbound connections. True kernel pre-connect Ask remains the next major stage.</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.TrueDelete">Safe Del: hidden WFP quarantine after removing a row</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.TrueDelete.Info">In Normal + GeniaFirewall WFP, the row really disappears, while the Service keeps a hidden ASK-BLOCK for that EXE. On the next network activity the application reappears as Pending decision.</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Service.Group">WFP system service</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Service.Info">The service is extracted from the portable EXE only into a protected Program Files directory. Only SYSTEM and Administrators may write there. Deactivation first performs a verified WFP policy clear and switches the backend to Compatibility.</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Service.Activate">Activate</sys:String>
    <sys:String xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime" x:Key="Settings.Service.Deactivate">Deactivate</sys:String>
